'''''Herbertus''''' is a genus of [[Marchantiophyta|liverworts]] in the family [[Herbertaceae]]. The genus has a broad global or [[cosmopolitan distribution]],<ref name="GBIF">{{cite web |title=''Herbertus'' Gray |url=https://www.gbif.org/species/2689385 |website=www.gbif.org |access-date=26 June 2023 |language=en}}</ref> including sixteen species that occur in [[Eurasia]]:<ref name="Bell">{{cite journal |author=David Bell & David Long deek |year=2012 |title=European ''Herbertus'' and the 'Viking prongwort' |journal=Field Bryology |volume=106 |pages=3–14 |url=http://rbg-web2.rbge.org.uk/bbs/Activities/field%20bryology/FB106/FB106%20Bell%20Long.pdf |format=[[Portable Document Format|PDF]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite journal |author=Aino Juslén |year=2006 |title=Revision of Asian ''Herbertus'' (Herbertaceae, Marchantiophyta) |journal=[[Annales Botanici Fennici]] |volume=43 |issue=6 |pages=409–436 |url=http://www.sekj.org/PDF/anbf43/anbf43-409.pdf |format=[[Portable Document Format|PDF]]}}</ref>

